{
  // @title: tsconfig.tests - strict TypeScript over the test tree and the hosted files it exercises, with the debt recorded not hidden.
  // @state: the count of errors under this project is ratchet-gated by scripts/verify/type-debt.ts; it may only go down.
  // @dependencies: tsconfig.base.json, scripts/verify/type-debt.ts.
  // WHY THE DEBT IS RECORDED HERE AND NOT FIXED BY HAND IN ONE DIFF.
  // tests/ was written in JavaScript-flavoured TypeScript before the tree was ever strict; the 2026-11-17 migration measured 1796 errors.
  // Fixing them in one change would be unreviewable and unverifiable; this gate makes the debt first-class so every subsequent change must leave it the same or smaller.
  // The clean surfaces (shared, local, extension, scripts, site) stay pinned at zero in tsconfig.tooling.json; only this project holds the grandfathered debt.
  "extends": "./tsconfig.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true,
    "allowImportingTsExtensions": true,
    "erasableSyntaxOnly": true,
    "types": [
      "node",
      "chrome"
    ]
  },
  "include": [
    "tests/**/*.ts",
    "extension/types/**/*.d.ts"
  ]
}
